# Trivy ignore file for CYO Adventure container image scanning.
#
# Scope: ONLY base-image (Debian trixie) OS-package CVEs that currently have NO
# fixed version available upstream. Every entry below was confirmed via
#   trivy image --scanners vuln --severity CRITICAL,HIGH <image>
# to report an empty "Fixed Version" with status "affected" or "fix_deferred".
#
# Policy (per CLAUDE.md "Unfixed CVEs"): these are not suppressions of fixable
# issues. They are unavoidable until Debian ships patched packages. Re-evaluate
# on each base-image bump; remove any entry once a fixed version lands, and let
# the patched package flow in via the runtime stage `apt-get upgrade`.
#
# Remediation already applied in the Dockerfile (so these do NOT need ignores):
#   - curl / libcurl4t64 / libssh2-1t64 CVEs: curl is no longer installed.
#   - openssl / libssl CVE-2026-45447: resolved by `apt-get upgrade`.
#   - Go stdlib / esbuild CVEs: frontend/node_modules excluded via .dockerignore.
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-08-14 (added the nine linux-libc-dev kernel-header CVEs
# from the PR #709 Trivy run; see the block at the end of this file)
# Previously: 2026-08-08 (added the single-CVE linux-libc-dev CVE-2026-68480
# block from the PR #644 Container Security run. Note that the 2026-08-04 review
# which added CVE-2026-64561 did not bump this stamp; it is folded in here rather
# than backdated, so this line now covers both. Prior review 2026-08-02: added
# the single-CVE linux-libc-dev 6.12.100-1+dhi0
# block from the PR #547 Container Security run. CVE-2026-64530 and
# CVE-2026-64531 were never added here: they were fixed outright by that same
# base-image digest bump, which is why they are recorded in
# docs/known-vulnerabilities.md as resolved rather than accepted. Prior review
# 2026-07-30: added the 7-CVE linux-libc-dev block from the PR #494 Container
# Security run; removed the CVE-2026-53399 / CVE-2026-64600 block, whose own
# removal condition was met when the dhi-python:3.14-debian13 base advanced from
# 6.12.95-1+dhi0 to 6.12.96-1+dhi0, the version Debian records as fixing both.
# gawk block 2026-07-14). See each block's own "Confirmed via" comment below for
# when it was individually last re-verified against a live Trivy run.

